cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "GalleyTeX: Word-to-LaTeX manuscript typesetting with author-in-the-loop proofreading"
abstract: >-
  GalleyTeX converts Word (.docx) manuscripts into compilable LaTeX projects for
  journal and conference submission systems. It converts Word equations (OMML)
  to LaTeX, maps template heading styles and manually formatted headings to
  section levels, renders merged table cells, links in-text citations to the
  reference list, and degrades unconvertible content (legacy equation-editor
  objects, native charts, metafile images) to visible placeholders so that the
  exported project always compiles. A single-file offline web application lets
  authors who do not know LaTeX proofread and correct every recognised block,
  including equations, before the project is handed to the editorial office.
